Fix djasm.y's K&R forward declaration of sortsyms() under gcc 15.

gcc 15 defaults to -std=gnu23 where empty parens in a function
declaration mean "(void)", not "unspecified parameters". The existing
prototype `void sortsyms();` then conflicts with the later definition
and call sites that pass an int(*)(const void*, const void*).

Match the prototype to the definition to compile under any C standard.

--- a/src/djasm/djasm.y
+++ b/src/djasm/djasm.y
@@ -179,7 +179,7 @@
 void modrm(int mod, int reg, int rm);
 void reg(int reg);
 void addr32(int sib);
-void sortsyms();
+void sortsyms(int (*)(void const *, void const *));

 int istemp(char *symname, char which);
 int islocal(char *symname);
